hey everyone how's it going my name is  mayuko and welcome back to my channel it  has been a hot minute since i've made  any sort of like desk related video so  today i want to talk about my favorite  desk accessories by the way i'm also  going to be filming like an office tour  video as well as like some other gadget  review thing so if you're interested in  that kind of content then make sure to  subscribe so yeah i've made a bunch of  updates and not only that but i've also  kind of lived with these updates for a  few months at least and so i can  actually really talk about all these  things in depth about what i like about  them and sometimes what i don't like  about them i'm going to introduce a  bunch of these dust accessory things to  you today so let's get started by the  way i just want to call out thank you to  logitech for sponsoring today's video  i'm really excited to talk about their  products which are part of my new  favorite desk accessory so stay tuned  the first item that i want to talk about  are my felt right tiles these are the  tiles that you see right behind me  they're set up right on the wall behind  my monitor i really wanted to have  something that was more visually  pleasing to look at than just a white  wall i also didn't want something as  distracting as like artwork and wanted  something just a little bit more like to  add some textural and color variety to  my workspace so i thought about getting  sound tiles for a very long time because  then it also helps kind of stamp in my  room a little bit sound wise and then i  think i got like an instagram ad or  something for felt right and felt right  is this company that makes all these  sound dampening like things that are all  made of wool and so they have a bunch of  different styles and colors and shapes i  went for the hexagon ones but i know  they also have like subway tile  rectangular looking things as well a  bunch of different designs they were  super duper easy to install they just  use like double-sided tape i used  actually the cracking the coding  interview book as a spacer between all  of my tiles because i wanted them to be  uniform and i didn't know what else to  use in terms of the sound dampening  quality i wouldn't say that it's like  massive i mean this is just one  part of one wall of the four walls in my  room and so i wouldn't say that i've  noticed a huge drastic difference in the  sound itself it hasn't gotten worse like  the sound in my room hasn't gotten worse  it maybe has gotten better i have no way  to actually measure that like  objectively speaking but i do know that  these sometimes really do get used in  actual sound dampening applications and  what's cool about these is you can also  like pin things to them which i might do  at some point but i still just wanted to  keep it really nice and basic and the  colors are really pretty it matches all  the greenery in my room and so really  happy with how it turned out honestly  the next item that i want to talk about  is my elgato key light so i've been  wanting some sort of key light on my  desk for a while and i chose the elgato  one just because i knew that it was like  a really popular product and it has been  such an upgrade for my desk specifically  the thing that it's really helped with  is that it provides some good lighting  to my face when i'm in like video calls  or doing interviews and stuff like that  i don't have any good lighting from that  wall onto my face and so especially if  it's in the evening or something like  that it illuminates my face and kind of  like creates a nice soft glow i guess  you can connect this key light  wirelessly to your computer for controls  where you can adjust brightness and  warmth another thing that i really like  about this one is that it's got a really  minimal design and so i like that it's  kind of got this like rectangular shape  with rounded edges the build quality is  honestly really good and i got the  version that latches onto my desk the  head itself is like fully adjustable it  can swivel in every direction 360  whatever that is and so sometimes i'll  honestly just use it as a desk light but  yeah really great upgrade for me  especially because now is the age of  like zoom meetings and online meetings  sometimes at like five o'clock or six  o'clock or seven o'clock or just like  the sun goes down early and whatever so  really really great upgrade for my desk  the next item that i want to talk about  is my new keyboard which is the logitech  mx mechanical mini so i was on this  keyboard from logitech it's the brand  new mechanical keyboard from logitech i  was so so so excited to use this one  because y'all know i'm just a huge fan  of like logitech products in general so  i've used like every version of the mx  keys since like four years ago and i  really really like it and this keyboard  has honestly a lot of the same things  that i liked about the mx key and really  like any other logitech keyboard in  general because they're all really well  made so things like being able to  connect wirelessly through bluetooth or  the logibolt usb receiver the fact that  it can connect up to three devices it  charges with usbc no battery is required  and the keys are programmable and can  have app specific settings that last  part is actually like game changer like  literally being able to program my keys  to different apps specifically things  like premiere pro and coding ides has  made my workflow just so much smoother  and so the difference with this keyboard  is that the keys are mechanical and  honestly it's got that really nice  mechanical keyboard quality of like  tactileness and the sound but it's not  too loud  i chose the tactile quiet browns for  this one because i i know i like tactile  quiet keys but it also comes in a linear  red and a clicky blue the logitech mx  mechanical keyboard comes in two  different size factors one with a numpad  and the other without which is the one  that i have the thing to note about  these keys which i think like kind of  differentiates it from other mechanical  keyboards is that the keys are really  slim profile so it's almost as if you  could get like a like a slim profile  keyboard but the keys are mechanical  which i feel like in a lot of ways are  like the best of two worlds so yeah this  mechanical keyboard honestly so good  it's i think it's actually more like  full specced than most other mechanical  keyboards out there because of all the  features that logitech already brings to  all of their keyboards so if you're  looking for a mechanical keyboard you're  just looking to get into it then this is  a great keyboard the next time that i  want to talk about is again another  logitech product which is the mx master  3s so a logitech keyboard begs for a  logitech mouse because it's really the  combination of these two that really  unlock the true power of this ecosystem  i was using the mx master 3 for mac  prior to this and this does actually  really feel like a huge upgrade from the  previous one and specifically the thing  that i like the most like literally when  i used it for the first time i was i was  like so delighted i was like whoa okay  and that's the quiet click functionality  basically when you click using the right  or left button it's literally just so  quiet again this has all the features  that i've loved about the logitech mx  master series from all the previous  versions and improved upon it so things  like how you can charge it using a usb  connection honestly it doesn't need to  charge very often i maybe charge it like  once every two months i want to say and  the charging port is in the front of the  mouse so you can use it while you're  charging very underrated feature i gotta  say this one you can also connect  wirelessly to up to three devices using  bluetooth or the logi bolt receiver and  the thing that i was talking about about  like what makes it so powerful in  conjunction with the keyboard is that  it's also programmable and so you can  have basic settings as well as app  specific settings that really help your  workflow like truly i've gotten so much  faster at editing things to these two  products like it is a game changer the  other thing that i really really like  about this mouse is the color i had like  all the previous versions which were  like gray which is great but this one  comes in a beautiful uh like grayish  whitish color and i feel like it matches  the rest of my desk better and the  updates don't stop just at the color so  there's also a customizable pointer  speed now it tracks well on glass the  mouse itself is made from recycled  plastic it comes in responsible  packaging and it's a carbon neutral  product so yeah honestly this is another  just so such a good mouse so if you're  gonna buy one mouse buy this one the  next time i should come at no surprise  for my subscribers because it's my grove  made desk mat this is a long time  favorite i feel like i've talked about  it in almost every other desk setup  video this is a desk map that i put my  keyboard and mouse on made by grovemade  it's made of wool and i've used it for i  want to say like almost two years and  it's held up super well the wool  honestly has gotten softer over time and  so it's really actually kind of  comfortable to like put my hands on  think of it as like my home base that  creates like a house for like my  keyboard and mouse and it's nice that  it's just like it's comfy to like use as  well it doesn't pill at all it's just a  really high quality good product and the  other thing is that it just looks really  good on my desk too  just beautiful the next thing that i  want to talk about which i guess you'd  call it a desk accessory i'm going to  call it a dust accessory is my desktop  wallpaper so i kind of feel like  wallpaper choice is like underrated i  feel like having a good wallpaper on  your desktop especially when you have  such a huge screen like mine really kind  of helps set the tone and mood for  whatever you're doing at your desk the  wallpaper that i have is from kuroku and  it's from the taiyo series it was  actually made by my friend tom who runs  the channel bite review i saw this  wallpaper i think on his desk and i was  like dude where did you get that  wallpaper and then i found out that it  made it it comes in a variety of  different colors it's got really some  nice like organic shapes that kind of  remind you of nature but like not so  much that there's so much detail on it i  just think it looks really really nice  with the rest of my desk set up i  believe he also has a lot of other  wallpapers and stuff too and so  definitely check his stuff out and the  last desk accessory that i want to talk  about is my wireless charger so a lot of  our personal devices have some sort of  wireless charging functionality to it so  you know things like my iphone and my  airpods need charging all the time and  so i really like having this wireless  charger that i found on amazon on my  desk i really actually like the design  of it which is one of the main reasons  why i chose it the cross tells you  exactly where to put your device to make  sure that it charges and it has a small  indicator light to tell you if it's  charging or not plugs in the back with a  usbc connection and i just think it  blends really well with everything else  that's going on on my desk my primary  use for this is to charge my airpods  because as soon as i get out of like a  zoom meeting or something like that and  i take my air pods out i put it on the  case and then i just set it on the  wireless charger to make sure that it's  charged for my next session so i'm like  never out of airpod battery i've had  this for like i want to say at least a  year and i have had zero problems with  it and so  honestly a great product alright so  those are all of my favorite desk  accessories let me know what you thought  in the comments down below and if  there's any parts of my desk setup  itself that you want me to cover in an  independent video i'll leave links for  everything in the description box down  below and i also want to thank logitech  again for sending me those products and  sponsoring this video don't forget to  subscribe to my channel and i will see  you next time bye  [Music]

